module

public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Presheaf.Sheafification
public import Mathlib.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.PushforwardContinuous
public import Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Sites.LocallyBijective
public import StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.TensorCoherence
public import StacksCore.Tactic.StacksAttribute

/-!
# Sheafification of presheaves of modules commutes with restriction to a slice site

Let `R` be a sheaf of rings on a site `(C, J)` and let `U : C`. Restriction of presheaves of
modules to the slice site `(Over U, J.over U)` is Mathlib's `PresheafOfModules.pushforward`
along `Over.forget U` with no change of scalars, and this file shows that it commutes with
sheafification:

`(P|_U)^# ≅ (P^#)|_U`.

The proof is the one Stacks uses for the localization of a topos: the sheafification unit
`P ⟶ P^#` stays locally bijective after restriction, because `Over.forget U` is cocontinuous,
so the morphism adjoint to the restricted unit is an isomorphism.

This is the last piece of infrastructure needed to transport generation by `r` sections through
extension of scalars, i.e. for [Stacks, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)(6)
and its pullback statement
[Stacks, Tag 03DO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DO): "locally generated by `r`
sections" is a statement about the slice sites, while extension of scalars is defined by a
sheafification on the ambient site, so the two must be interchanged.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification.presheafOverFunctor`: restriction of presheaves of
  modules to the slice site over `U`.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification.restrictedUnit` and `overToSheafify`: the
  sheafification unit restricted to the slice site, as a morphism of presheaves of modules and
  as a morphism of the underlying presheaves of abelian groups.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification.sheafifyOverHom`: the comparison morphism, adjoint
  to `restrictedUnit`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification.isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm`: a locally
  bijective morphism from a presheaf of modules into a sheaf of modules exhibits the latter as
  the sheafification of the former. This is `Stacks.TensorCoherence
  .isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm` with the ring universe freed; see the implementation notes.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification.isLocallySurjective_overToSheafify` and
  `isLocallyInjective_overToSheafify`: the restricted sheafification unit is still locally
  bijective, because `Over.forget U` is cocontinuous.
* `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification.isIso_sheafifyOverHom` and `sheafifyOverIso`:
  **sheafification commutes with restriction to a slice site.**

## Implementation notes

**Relation to what is already here.** `Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceRestriction.sliceSheafifyIso`
(in `StacksFrontier.Algebra.Category.ModuleCat.Sheaf.SliceRestrictionMonoidal`) is the same
mathematics for a *commutative* ring presheaf: it is indexed by `𝒪 : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ CommRingCat`
together with a proof that `Stacks.SheafOfModules.TensorSheafification.structureRingPresheaf 𝒪` is
  a sheaf, and it is stated as
a natural isomorphism of functors in that spelling. `Stacks.TensorCoherence.tensorSheafOverIso`
is the tensor-specific instance of the same comparison. Neither applies to an arbitrary sheaf of
rings `R : Sheaf J RingCat`, which is the generality the change-of-scalars argument needs, so
the statement here is strictly more general than both; a dedup against `sliceSheafifyIso` is
owed if the commutative development is ever restated over `Sheaf J RingCat`.

**One spelling per statement, and why local bijectivity is taken as an explicit hypothesis.**
`overToSheafify` is a `def` with an *ascribed* type, and `isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm`
takes local injectivity and surjectivity as explicit arguments rather than as instances. This is
not stylistic. The target of the restricted unit has two definitionally equal spellings,
`((P^#).over U).val.presheaf` and `(PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (R.over U).obj).obj
((P^#).over U).val`, and typeclass synthesis distinguishes them: Mathlib's
`CategoryTheory.Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_of_isLocallySurjective_fac` takes its
local-surjectivity hypothesis as an *instance*, and routed through it this proof has the
hypothesis in the context in one spelling while the synthesis goal demands the other —
resolution then fails on two types that print identically. With the hypotheses explicit the
check is a single tolerant defeq test.

For the same reason every implicit argument of `isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm` is supplied
by name at the one place it is applied. Leaving `Rs` to be inferred poses the unification
problem `?Rs.obj =?= (R.over U).obj` — a metavariable under a projection — and that exhausts
the heartbeat budget in `whnf` *in the application*, not in any proof.

**Universes.** Four, all independent: the site `C : Type u` with `Category.{v} C`, the sheaf of
rings at `RingCat.{t}`, and the modules at `PresheafOfModules.{w}`. The ring universe `t` and the
module universe `w` are independent in Mathlib's `PresheafOfModules.sheafification`, so no
`max` is forced and nothing is narrowed; this is case 1 of the universe diagnostic — `t` is a
parameter the statements merely carry. `Stacks.TensorCoherence
.isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm` would have discharged `isIso_sheafifyOverHom` directly, but
it ties the ring universe to the module universe; its proof is reproduced here with `t` free,
reusing `Stacks.TensorCoherence.isIso_homEquiv_symm`, which is already universe-polymorphic.
The slice site `Over U` lives in `Type (max u v)`; that is a change of site, not a narrowing of
a universe parameter.

**Hypotheses.** Beyond the site and the sheaf of rings these are `HasWeakSheafify` and
`WEqualsLocallyBijective` for `AddCommGrpCat.{w}`, on `J` and on `J.over U` — exactly what the
two sheafification functors need. No `GrothendieckTopology.HasSheafCompose` instance is
required, and no hypothesis on `C` beyond being a category: in particular no finite limits and
no products, so nothing here acquires `HasBinaryProducts C`.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 00XB](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/00XB) — the localized site
  `C/U`.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DL](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DL)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 03DO](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/03DO)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory Limits

universe w t v u

namespace Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification

section Uniqueness

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  {R₀ : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{t}} {Rs : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}} (α : R₀ ⟶ Rs.obj)
  [Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J α] [Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J α]
  [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- A locally bijective morphism from a presheaf of modules into (the restriction of scalars of)
a sheaf of modules exhibits the latter as the sheafification of the former.

This is `Stacks.TensorCoherence.isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm` with the ring universe `t`
independent of the module universe `w`; the proof is the same, and the dedup is owed if that
statement is ever generalized. -/
theorem isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm {P : PresheafOfModules.{w} R₀}
    {T : SheafOfModules.{w} Rs}
    (u : P ⟶ (SheafOfModules.forget Rs ⋙ PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars α).obj T)
    (hinj : Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R₀).map u))
    (hsurj : Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective J ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R₀).map u)) :
    IsIso ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv α).symm u) := by
  have := hinj
  have := hsurj
  rw [← isIso_iff_of_reflects_iso _ (SheafOfModules.toSheaf.{w} Rs),
    PresheafOfModules.toSheaf_map_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm]
  have h : IsIso ((presheafToSheaf J AddCommGrpCat.{w}).map
      ((PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf R₀).map u)) :=
    (J.W_iff _).1 (J.W_of_isLocallyBijective _)
  exact Stacks.TensorCoherence.isIso_homEquiv_symm _ _ h

end Uniqueness

section Slice

variable {C : Type u} [Category.{v} C] {J : GrothendieckTopology C}
  (R : Sheaf J RingCat.{t}) (U : C)

/-- Restriction of presheaves of modules to the slice site over `U`: Mathlib's pushforward
along `Over.forget U`, with no change of scalars. -/
noncomputable abbrev presheafOverFunctor :
    PresheafOfModules.{w} R.obj ⥤ PresheafOfModules.{w} (R.over U).obj :=
  PresheafOfModules.pushforward.{w} (F := Over.forget U) (𝟙 (R.over U).obj)

variable [HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{w}] [J.WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  (P : PresheafOfModules.{w} R.obj)

/-- The sheafification unit `P ⟶ P^#` restricted to the slice site over `U`, as a morphism of
presheaves of `R|_U`-modules. Its components are the components of the unit at the objects
`Over.forget U V`. -/
noncomputable def restrictedUnit :
    (presheafOverFunctor.{w} R U).obj P ⟶
      (PresheafOfModules.restrictScalars (𝟙 (R.over U).obj)).obj
        (((PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).obj P).over U).val where
  app V := ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).unit.app P).app
    ((Over.forget U).op.obj V)
  naturality f := ((PresheafOfModules.sheafificationAdjunction.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).unit.app P).naturality
    ((Over.forget U).op.map f)

/-- The restricted sheafification unit at the level of the underlying presheaves of abelian
groups. The type is ascribed so that the target is spelled through
`PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf`, which is the spelling the factorization `sheafifyOverHom_fac`
produces. -/
noncomputable def overToSheafify :
    ((presheafOverFunctor.{w} R U).obj P).presheaf ⟶
      (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (R.over U).obj).obj
        (((PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).obj P).over U).val :=
  (PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf (R.over U).obj).map (restrictedUnit.{w} R U P)

/-- `overToSheafify` is the whiskering of the sheafification unit along `Over.forget U`. -/
theorem overToSheafify_eq : overToSheafify.{w} R U P =
    Functor.whiskerLeft (Over.forget U).op (CategoryTheory.toSheafify J P.presheaf) :=
  rfl

/-- The restricted sheafification unit is locally surjective: `Over.forget U` is cocontinuous,
so local surjectivity restricts to the slice site. -/
theorem isLocallySurjective_overToSheafify :
    Presheaf.IsLocallySurjective (J.over U) (overToSheafify.{w} R U P) := by
  rw [overToSheafify_eq]
  exact Presheaf.isLocallySurjective_whisker (J.over U) J (Over.forget U) _

/-- The restricted sheafification unit is locally injective. -/
theorem isLocallyInjective_overToSheafify :
    Presheaf.IsLocallyInjective (J.over U) (overToSheafify.{w} R U P) := by
  rw [overToSheafify_eq]
  exact Presheaf.isLocallyInjective_whisker (J.over U) J (Over.forget U) _

variable [HasWeakSheafify (J.over U) AddCommGrpCat.{w}]
  [(J.over U).WEqualsLocallyBijective AddCommGrpCat.{w}]

/-- The comparison morphism from the sheafification over the slice site of the restriction of
`P` to the restriction of the sheafification of `P`: the morphism adjoint to the restricted
sheafification unit. -/
noncomputable def sheafifyOverHom :
    (PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 (R.over U).obj)).obj
        ((presheafOverFunctor.{w} R U).obj P) ⟶
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).obj P).over U :=
  (PresheafOfModules.sheafificationHomEquiv (𝟙 (R.over U).obj)).symm (restrictedUnit.{w} R U P)

/-- The comparison morphism `sheafifyOverHom` is an isomorphism. -/
instance isIso_sheafifyOverHom : IsIso (sheafifyOverHom.{w} R U P) :=
  isIso_sheafificationHomEquiv_symm.{w} (R₀ := (R.over U).obj) (Rs := R.over U)
    (P := (presheafOverFunctor.{w} R U).obj P)
    (T := ((PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).obj P).over U)
    (𝟙 (R.over U).obj) (restrictedUnit.{w} R U P)
    (isLocallyInjective_overToSheafify.{w} R U P) (isLocallySurjective_overToSheafify.{w} R U P)

/-- **Sheafification of presheaves of modules commutes with restriction to a slice site.**
The sheafification over `Over U` of the restriction of `P` is the restriction of the
sheafification of `P`. -/
noncomputable def sheafifyOverIso :
    (PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 (R.over U).obj)).obj
        ((presheafOverFunctor.{w} R U).obj P) ≅
      ((PresheafOfModules.sheafification.{w} (𝟙 R.obj)).obj P).over U :=
  asIso (sheafifyOverHom.{w} R U P)

end Slice

end Stacks.SheafOfModules.SliceSheafification

end
